Expose the AVI backend through the existing CRT-bypass launcher.
DD2_MOVIE runs the real Init_Application / Sound_Remove / Set_Draw_Mode(1) /
Play_Movie sequence rather than a decoder-only fixture. It is a diagnostic
entry for complete native/browser MCI sink and skip/completion comparisons.
The deterministic race/FE fixtures retain their original entry sequence.
This launcher change does not modify reconstructed engine instructions.

--- a/dd2_runtime.c
+++ b/dd2_runtime.c
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@
     { unsigned va; for(va=0x46c330; va<=0x46c364; va+=4) *(int*)(uintptr_t)va = (int)(long)&dd2_crt_lock; }
     __InitRtns();
     dd2_com_init();
+    if(getenv("DD2_MOVIE")) {
+        extern int dd2_movie_run(const char*);
+        return dd2_movie_run(getenv("DD2_MOVIE"));
+    }
